ome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_011vNtXthW4U4nkmDHdEWbLy", "tool": "open_pr_legacy", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 397941, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_011vNtXthW4U4nkmDHdEWbLy", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 402957, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money`'s docstring says it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but the code used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. So 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66, which made `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` fail.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I committed a change that switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. The main PR tool kept returning \"503 Service Unavailable\" and didn't create anything. I confirmed there were no open PRs, then opened it through the legacy PR tool, so there's only one.\n\nI haven't merged it. That needs approval from a code owner.\n\nI couldn't find FIN-212 in the advisory lookup (\"Unknown advisory\"). It's probably an internal finance requirement, not a security advisory. I went with the test and the existing docstring, which both say ROUND_HALF_EVEN.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015BNpfTETKh4LGdBiYXpksz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Jkdrs35yEAuDAt5Zsr5pGQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file